NNAAMMEE
     yyppwwhhiicchh — return hostname of NIS server of map master

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     yyppwwhhiicchh [--dd _d_o_m_a_i_n] [[--tt] --mm [_m_n_a_m_e] | _h_o_s_t]
     yyppwwhhiicchh --xx

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The yyppwwhhiicchh utility tells which NIS server supplies NIS services to a
     client, or which is the master for a map.  If invoked without arguments,
     it gives the NIS server for the local machine.  If _h_o_s_t is specified,
     that machine is queried to find out which NIS server it is using.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd _d_o_m_a_i_n
             Specify a domain other than the default domain.

     --tt      Inhibit translation of map nicknames to their corresponding map
             names.

     --mm [_m_n_a_m_e]
             Find the master NIS server for the named map.  No _h_o_s_t may be
             specified with the --mm option.  The _m_n_a_m_e argument can be a map
             name or nickname.  If _m_n_a_m_e is omitted, yyppwwhhiicchh will produce a
             list of available maps.

     --xx      Display the map nickname table.

